        "original_id": "9869fb42-4275-547a-a5ab-19c9421a9021",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Sky Rocket, Phantom's Revenge, Steel Phantom\n- Places: Kennywood Park, Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania\n- Topics: roller coasters, inversions, park renovation, record-breaking rides\n\nFacts:\n- In 1991, Phantom's Revenge opened as the fastest roller coaster in the world and had the longest drop of any roller coaster in the world.\n- In 2001, Kennywood Park renovated Steel Phantom into Phantom's Revenge.\n- Sky Rocket is a steel roller coaster located at Kennywood Park in Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania.\n- Sky Rocket was the first coaster erected at Kennywood Park after the 2001 renovation of Steel Phantom into Phantom's Revenge.\n- Sky Rocket marked the return to Kennywood Park of a roller coaster that features inversions.",
